From 65fb0ebb4adf072eff0fdc8797335babd45154fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:06:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] feat(control-plane): select the runtime launcher from
 the environment

The app needs one place that turns configuration into a launcher and
refuses to start on anything it cannot honour, like the inventory and
auth settings do. launcher_from_env(inventory) reads:

- FORGEMESH_RUNTIME_LAUNCHER: `fake` or `vllm-process` (case
  insensitive); unset or blank selects none; any other value is
  refused, and so is a launcher without FORGEMESH_INVENTORY_FILE,
  because then no service could ever be scheduled.
- fake: FORGEMESH_FAKE_LAUNCHER_BIND_HOST (default 127.0.0.1) and
  FORGEMESH_FAKE_LAUNCHER_ADVERTISE_HOST (default: the bind host,
  required when binding all addresses).
- vllm-process: FORGEMESH_VLLM_COMMAND (shell-style split, no shell;
  default `<python> -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server`, which needs
  the vllm package for this interpreter), FORGEMESH_VLLM_BIND_HOST,
  FORGEMESH_VLLM_ADVERTISE_HOST, FORGEMESH_VLLM_READY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
  (default 1200) and FORGEMESH_VLLM_STOP_GRACE_SECONDS (default 10).

Because vLLM instances run on the control plane host, vllm-process
also requires an inventory with exactly one node whose device ids all
map to distinct CUDA devices; `0` and `gpu-0` naming the same GPU would
let two services share it.

Settings of the launcher that is not selected are not read. Every error
names the variable to fix.
